   "he": "הַכֶּלֶב שֶׁנָּטַל.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: With regard to «a dog that took» a cake that had been baked directly on hot coals, and went to a stack of grain to eat it, and it ate the cake and at the same time ignited the stack of grain with a coal that it had taken along with the cake, the owner of the dog must pay the full cost of the damage for the cake, and he must pay for half the cost of the damage to the stack of grain."
  }
